    blurb: 'Soft, plucked chords with a round attack and a short ring.',
    how: 'A single sawtooth through the 2-pole filter, with the filter envelope doing the plucking: it opens the filter at the start of each note and lets it close while the note rings on. The loudness envelope keeps some sustain, so held chords stay present but darker.',
